.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-set 1  "rev-stealth-config-set " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-set \- P6.3: Set a dotted\-path key on `policy.toml` (or another target file) to a value. Type is inferred from the literal text (`true`/`false` → bool, all\-digits → int, otherwise string). The value is written through the atomic ConfigWriter only after the resulting document passes strict validation. Secret values are NOT echoed back
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config set\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a dotted\-path key on policy.toml (or another target file). Type is inferred from the literal text. Writes go through the atomic ConfigWriter after strict validation. Secret values are NOT echoed back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR [default: policy]
Which file to mutate. Defaults to `policy`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
policy
.IP \(bu 2
authorized
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Dotted key, e.g. `policy.require_vpn` or `require_vpn`. A leading `policy.` / `authorized.` segment is treated as a layer hint and stripped before traversing the TOML document
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
Value as a literal token. Inferred as bool (`true`/`false`), int (all\-digits, optional leading `\-`), or string (everything else). To force string mode wrap the value in quotes from the shell
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config set policy.require_vpn true
  $ rev\-stealth config set vpn.cooldown_seconds 30 \-\-target policy
  $ rev\-stealth config set hosts.allow_x_test true \-\-target authorized

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Key set and file committed.
  1  UserError        Bad key / type mismatch / validation failure.
  3  PermanentError   ConfigWriter IO failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_POLICY      Override the policy.toml path.
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTHORIZED  Override the authorized.toml path.
